NOT CORRECT yet. I can see exactly what happened: your Stage 10 is still duplicated. For example, the second docker run -d appears in the diff. So do not commit or push.

Let's stop using the downloaded file and manual editing. We'll fix the file directly from Git's clean version with one command sequence. This avoids all the copy/paste mistakes.

1. First, reset the Jenkinsfile

Run:

git checkout HEAD -- .\CI\Jenkinsfile

Then verify:

git status --porcelain

It should return nothing.

2. Run this exact PowerShell script

Copy the whole block at once:

$path = ".\CI\Jenkinsfile"

# Get the clean Jenkinsfile directly from Git
$content = git show HEAD:CI/Jenkinsfile | Out-String

# Locate Stage 10 and Stage 11
$startPattern = '(?ms)        // 10\. START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER.*?(?=        // 11\. BACKEND HEALTH CHECK)'
$match = [regex]::Match($content, $startPattern)

if (-not $match.Success) {
    throw "Stage 10 was not found."
}

$newStage = @"
        // 10. START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER
        // ============================================================
        stage('Start Backend Test Container') {
            steps {

                withCredentials([
                    string(
                        credentialsId: 'cag-website-v2-ci-encryption-key',
                        variable: 'ENCRYPTION_KEY'
                    )
                ]) {

                    sh '''
                        set -e

                        echo "=============================================="
                        echo "START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER"
                        echo "=============================================="

                        docker run -d \
                            --name "\${BACKEND_CONTAINER}" \
                            --network "\${CI_NETWORK}" \
                            -e ENVIRONMENT=production \
                            -e ENCRYPTION_KEY="\${ENCRYPTION_KEY}" \
                            -e DB_HOST=postgres \
                            -e DB_PORT=5432 \
                            -e DB_NAME="\${POSTGRES_DB}" \
                            -e DB_USER="\${POSTGRES_USER}" \
                            -e DB_PASSWORD="\${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}" \
                            -e DB_SCHEMA=cag_new \
                            -e DATABASE_URL="postgresql+psycopg2://\${POSTGRES_USER}:\${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/\${POSTGRES_DB}" \
                            "\${BACKEND_IMAGE}:\${GIT_COMMIT}"

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend container started:"

                        docker ps \
                            --filter "name=\${BACKEND_CONTAINER}"

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend image:"

                        docker inspect \
                            "\${BACKEND_CONTAINER}" \
                            --format '{{.Config.Image}}'

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend container started successfully."
                    '''
                }
            }
        }

"@

# Replace ONLY Stage 10
$content = $content.Remove($match.Index, $match.Length)
$content = $content.Insert($match.Index, $newStage)

# Write without BOM
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(
    (Resolve-Path $path),
    $content.TrimEnd() + "`n",
    [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)
)

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "Stage 10 replaced successfully."
3. Now check it

Run:

git diff --check

Then:

git diff -- CI/Jenkinsfile
4. Check for duplicates

Run these:

Select-String -Path .\CI\Jenkinsfile -Pattern "stage\('Start Backend Test Container'\)"

Must return exactly 1 line.

Select-String -Path .\CI\Jenkinsfile -Pattern "cag-website-v2-ci-encryption-key"

Must return exactly 1 line.

Select-String -Path .\CI\Jenkinsfile -Pattern 'ENCRYPTION_KEY="\$\{ENCRYPTION_KEY\}"'

Must return exactly 1 line.

And this:

Select-String -Path .\CI\Jenkinsfile -Pattern "START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER"

It should return 2 lines because one is the comment/header and one is the echo message. That's normal.

5. Most important check

Run:

git diff --numstat -- CI/Jenkinsfile

We expect approximately:

<some number>    <some number>    CI/Jenkinsfile

but not hundreds of changed lines.

The final Stage 10 must have only one:

docker run -d \

and only one:

docker inspect \

Your original clean Stage 10 has one backend container launch and one inspect operation.

