Yes — now I can see exactly what went wrong.

Your Stage 10 replacement is still wrong. The problem is this:

$newStage = @"

Because @"..."@ is a double-quoted PowerShell here-string, PowerShell expanded ${BACKEND_CONTAINER}, ${CI_NETWORK}, etc. before writing the Jenkinsfile. That is why your diff became:

--name "\" 
--network "\"
-e ENCRYPTION_KEY="\"

Also, the Stage 10 content became duplicated. Your uploaded output clearly shows this corruption.

Do this exactly — don't manually edit Jenkinsfile
Step 1 — Paste this entire block into PowerShell
# ============================================================
# FIX CI/Jenkinsfile STAGE 10
# ============================================================

$path = ".\CI\Jenkinsfile"

# 1. Restore Jenkinsfile to the clean committed version
git checkout HEAD -- .\CI\Jenkinsfile

# 2. Read the clean Jenkinsfile
$content = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText((Resolve-Path $path))

# 3. Locate Stage 10 and Stage 11
$startMarker = "        // 10. START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER"
$endMarker   = "        // 11. BACKEND HEALTH CHECK"

$startIndex = $content.IndexOf($startMarker)
$endIndex   = $content.IndexOf($endMarker)

if ($startIndex -lt 0) {
    throw "ERROR: Stage 10 start marker was not found."
}

if ($endIndex -lt 0) {
    throw "ERROR: Stage 11 marker was not found."
}

if ($endIndex -le $startIndex) {
    throw "ERROR: Stage 11 appears before Stage 10."
}

# ============================================================
# IMPORTANT:
# Use SINGLE-QUOTED here-string @' '@
# so PowerShell DOES NOT expand ${VARIABLES}
# ============================================================

$newStage = @'
        // ============================================================
        // 10. START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER
        // ============================================================
        stage('Start Backend Test Container') {
            steps {

                withCredentials([
                    string(
                        credentialsId: 'cag-website-v2-ci-encryption-key',
                        variable: 'ENCRYPTION_KEY'
                    )
                ]) {

                    sh '''
                        set -e

                        echo "=============================================="
                        echo "START BACKEND TEST CONTAINER"
                        echo "=============================================="

                        docker run -d \
                            --name "${BACKEND_CONTAINER}" \
                            --network "${CI_NETWORK}" \
                            -e ENVIRONMENT=production \
                            -e ENCRYPTION_KEY="${ENCRYPTION_KEY}" \
                            -e DB_HOST=postgres \
                            -e DB_PORT=5432 \
                            -e DB_NAME="${POSTGRES_DB}" \
                            -e DB_USER="${POSTGRES_USER}" \
                            -e DB_PASSWORD="${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}" \
                            -e DB_SCHEMA=cag_new \
                            -e DATABASE_URL="postgresql+psycopg2://${POSTGRES_USER}:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/${POSTGRES_DB}" \
                            "${BACKEND_IMAGE}:${GIT_COMMIT}"

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend container started:"

                        docker ps \
                            --filter "name=${BACKEND_CONTAINER}"

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend image:"

                        docker inspect \
                            "${BACKEND_CONTAINER}" \
                            --format '{{.Config.Image}}'

                        echo ""
                        echo "Backend container started successfully."

                        # IMPORTANT:
                        # Do NOT use:
                        # docker inspect <container> --format '{{.Os}}/{{.Architecture}}'
                        #
                        # Container inspect does not expose these image
                        # platform fields in this template.
                        #
                        # Architecture was already verified during
                        # docker image inspect in the build stage.
                    '''
                }
            }
        }

'@

# 4. Match the line endings of the existing Jenkinsfile
if ($content.Contains("`r`n")) {
    $newStage = $newStage -replace "`r?`n", "`r`n"
}
else {
    $newStage = $newStage -replace "`r?`n", "`n"
}

# 5. Replace ONLY Stage 10
$content = `
    $content.Substring(0, $startIndex) +
    $newStage +
    $content.Substring($endIndex)

# 6. Write the file
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(
    (Resolve-Path $path),
    $content,
    [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)
)

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "=============================================="
Write-Host "Stage 10 replacement completed."
Write-Host "=============================================="
Step 2 — Immediately run these validation commands

